# top-left command strip (2do task #4). Defaults match what's written
# below, so editing here is the only thing needed to change labels or
# commands - no recompile. Submenu rows: strip_btn_N_menu_M_label / _cmd.
# A row with a label and an empty command is a real "cancel" (click just
# dismisses). Commands are run via setsid nohup from house_root (§F-18).
# strip_x_offset scoots the whole strip right from the left screen edge.
# strip_y_offset scoots the whole strip down from the top screen edge -
# defaults to 40 (below GNOME Shell's own native top panel), direct
# instruction 2026-08-09.
# strip_user_cmd runs when the user/guest button is clicked (a no-op until
# wired to a user-switcher - DIRECT INSTRUCTION 2026-08-08).
SECTION      | strip_x_offset         | 200
SECTION      | strip_y_offset         | 50
SECTION      | strip_user_cmd         |
SECTION      | datetime_lang          | zh
SECTION      | strip_btn_0_label       | file
